node_modules
**/out
**/data
**/dist

# Nothing Sierra made is committed to this repository. Not the game resources,
# not pictures of them running. The engine is this project's; the games it runs
# are not, and a public repository that carries them is redistributing them.
#
# This rule used to name `web-agi/public/game/` -- the singular path the bundled
# copy lived at before M18's picker moved it to `games/`. The rename left the
# rule pointing at nothing, and two games' worth of resources were committed
# through the hole it left. Hence the trailing-slash-free globs below: they
# match wherever the directory sits.

# Game resources, copied in by `npm run game:sync`. Run it after cloning.
web-agi/public/games/
public/games/

# Screen captures of the original interpreter, read by the Hercules and CGA
# comparison tests. Those tests skip when these are absent, which is the normal
# case for a clone; put your own captures here to run them.
web-agi/test/captures/
test/captures/
screenshots-from-original

# Where `npm run logic:dump` puts a game's scripts. Regenerated, never read by
# anything that runs; it is there to be grepped while working out a puzzle.
web-agi/.logic/
